brendon.oliver@gmail.com writes:

> Just by the by, do you know of any resource which documents what can &
> can't be installed in the 64bit slots on the PWS500au?  I've had Matrox
> video cards, an Intel network card and an Adaptec 29160 SCSI card in
> some of those slots from time to time with no problem.

The bug occurs when a DMA transfer to the card (DMA read), crosses a
page boundary (8k).  For a video card, the only possible damage would
be a few pixels with wrong colors, and they don't use DMA very much in
the first place.  Since the MTU of normal Ethernet is less than 8k, I
would expect network cards to be safe as well.  Disk controllers
should be kept away from those slots, unless you are certain that all
transfers are safe.  This depends on the driver, not the card.

I don't know of any list of known-good cards.

