Actually, if you look at it just right, every edge of a
digital signal inside the computer is a pulse capable of
covering a wide frequency range.  The edges/pulses repeat
regularly, several million to a few billion times a second.
My AM broadcast headset radio picks up hash from my computer
at a few feet (a meter or so) away, even with all covers and
shields in place.  I wouldn't want to be in an apartment
next-door to someone who left covers or shields off.

> Just out of curiosity,
> do you happen to know what sort of damage the fence charger did?

Enough damage that the deer stayed away from the
landscaping.  I'm told one time a buck touched its nose to
the fence and jumped backward quite a distance.

Oh, did you mean the "damage" to radio communication?  :-)

Reportedly, it hashed out essentially all TV reception in
the whole neighborhood.  Not good.  :-(

