Hello,

  I am new to this group. I just acquired a Dec Alpha PC 164LX. Other
identifying information is Digital Alpha 21164 Rev 7.2 533 mhz 2 mb cache 256
mb Alpha Bios version 5.70 990720.1458. I need some help installing an OS and
getting this machine running.

  The previous owner had wiped the hard disk, probably to avoid any problems of
copyright infringement. When powering up the machine, it comes up with a bootup
menu. Both Linux and Windows 2000 were listed as choices. However, when I tried
selecting one of them, the initial startup logo showed, but then failed, saying
it could not find an OS. A screen came up inviting me to press F2 to enter
setup and configure the system, which I did. On the menu that came up, first I
chose "Hard Disk Setup", and chose the option to set up the disk for NT. Since
I have a copy of Windows NT 4.0 server, I decided to install that, since I know
it has a version for the Alpha. It created two FAT partitions. Next, I loaded
the NT CD in the drive and chose "Install Windows NT" from the setup menu. The
non-GUI part of the NT setup program started up. It seems to be going OK, for
about a minute. It is loading various drivers, and shows "Setup is Loading
Files" at the bottom of the window. It gets to the point where its loading the
file systems. Then, when it starts loading "CD-ROM File System", it hangs.
Sometimes it causes a blue screen of death. I have tried it numerous times, and
it always fails at the same place. I have also tried different Windows NT CD's.
Both the hard disk and CDROM are SCSI, if that matters. There are no IDE
devices installed in the system.

  Does anybody have a clue as to what is wrong? The procedure seems pretty
straightforward. Am I missing something? Is there something else I need to do?

  If installing NT on this machine fails, I have thought of installing Linux.
In fact, I have already ordered the Alpha version of Debian Linux. Can someone
tell me how to go about installing that on this machine? I have experience
installing Linux on 86 based machines, but not an Alpha.

  Also, I was really surprised to see that this machine had WIndows 2000
installed on it previously. I didn't think that Windows 2000 was ever available
for the Alpha. In fact, I have a Windows 2000 Professional CD, and I looked
over its directory structure and cannot find any "Alpha" directory, like on the
NT CD. Whats up with that?

  Thanks in advance for any help.

Tom


