I assume you are referring to the Digital Personal Workstation 500,
also known as the PWS500 or the Miata.

It takes PC100 or PC133 DIMMs with ECC, max 256MB per stick.  If you
go for 256MB modules, they need to be the kind with chips on both
sides.  The single-sided ones will not work.  Unfortunately, the
double-sided ones are hard to come by these days.

