Yea, I got DRI working. I got it working under Xfree86-4.3 to. It works like
a top with an ATI card, Matrox is unsupported. To get max speed I kind of
tweaked my XFree config though, included loading DRI/GLX/GLcore modules and
a few other little tweaks here and there.

As for my player, I was using Mplayer [compiled for the ev56]. I rolled it
into an rpm sometime ago, before my 'compile issues' with MplayerXP.
Acceleration also works under Xine but Mplayer runs cleaner. So far the
speed boost affected just about every multimedia player in have installed.

Running Gentoo? That shouldn't be an issue. Just download an install 'Alien'
[perl script] and you should be able to convert it to ordinary binaries
without a hitch. Xfree86 pretty much installs to the same location on just
about everyones setup. I think the defaults or such; /etc/X11:/usr/X11R6.

I compiled it using a elfloader patch [old as dirt] and using GCC-3.0.4. I
also tried it under GCC-3.4.3 but that was a no go. Heres the patch that I
used:

Bugreport: http://bugs.xfree86.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1568
Patch: http://bugs.xfree86.org/attachment.cgi?id=1356

