I put the whole 1,5GB RAM long time ago in PWS, so I didn't remember that
at first it all worked fine.
Time passed and these days the Miata has some problems at booting.
I took off the chassis cover and looked at the leds.
Many of the times, it stops at the D0 or D1 test, which (from manual)
points to a memory problem.
Today I went out and bought a CRC spray, went back and cleaned memory
slots and DIMMs as well.
Now the Miata boots fine every time and both SRM and Linux see all 1,5GB
RAM! :))

Yikes! Dust really matters. :)

