malakasoy <pana@gamithis.net> wrote:
> As a matter of interest, do you guys use these things for any real work, 
> or is it just a toy? I've installed openVMS on it and it runs fine, but 
> now i've got redhat linux and am trying to get mySQL running on it, but 
> it seems like it needs more than 128mb of ram to run properly.

My PWS500au (with one 18G U2W disk, an Elsa Glorias Synergy II
and 1.5GB of RAM runs very nicely (albeit a bit loud).

I use it mainly to test if some OSS software I maintain compiles
on Tru64 (which is what I'm running on it). Also, it gathers
assorted sensory data for digestion with RRD. I tried using it as
a proxy for me and my flatmates but that was a bit too much for
it. But that could also have been my ineptitude at tuning Squid.

One last job it has is showing off X11 on a real Unix to people
who have never seen it (hence the EGSII). Looks very nice on my
TFT :)

HTH,
Tobias

